Second flips: Ace of Wands—new fire sparks at the tip of a sprouting rod.  
Heat licks your palms, eager but not burning.

Third reveals: Two of Pentacles—coins orbit in an endless loop.  
Your pulse finds their rhythm, light and sure.

These cards are now yours. They hum in your memory.

The void thins. A seam of daylight cracks open.  
You step through; the world rushes in with salt wind and gull cries.

